head, 3 deep wide squat, 4 low crouch with a forearm near the cheek, 5 wide side lunge with one arm overhead, 6 raised-knee turn, 7 one-hand floor freeze, 8 rear-leg lift, 9 raised knee with both arms horizontal, 10 low directional push, 11 deep squat with one arm overhead, 12 lateral low stance, 13 seated floor lean, 14 standing arm extension, 15 knee lift with arms raised, and 16 wide diagonal reach. Transfer only the poses and movement order, not the source dancer's appearance or clothing.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] An exact 10-second, uncut photorealistic studio dance video. <Subject 1> preserves the identity and sportswear from <Picture 1> while performing all 16 poses from <Subject 2> in order. The choreography follows 16 beats at 96 BPM.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - face, bob haircut, athletic proportions, sports bra, leggings, and sneakers remain consistent.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1]): attribute_transfer - all 16 poses and their order transfer to <Subject 1>; the source dancer's face, hair, loose pants, watch, and clothing are ignored.\n\ndetailed_description:\nA high-end realistic dance-test video on a seamless white studio background, with soft high-key lighting, clean contact shadows, natural skin texture, and crisp fabric motion. The original character sheet and action contact sheet never appear in frame.\n\n[Shot 1] One continuous full-body shot runs from 00:00.000 to 00:10.000. <Subject 1> remains centered in frame, and a stabilized camera at a slight low angle performs only a restrained lateral orbit with a subtle push-in. No cuts, speed ramps, duplicated limbs, floating feet, identity changes, or extra people.\n\nFrom 00:00.000 to 00:02.500, covering beats 1-4, she moves from the neutral preparation into <Subject 2>'s wide lunge with one hand behind her head, then descends into the deep wide squat and folds into the low crouch with a forearm beside her cheek.\n\nFrom 00:02.500 to 00:05.000, covering beats 5-8, she opens into the wide side lunge with one arm overhead, snaps upward through the raised-knee turn, lowers into the one-hand floor freeze, and drives back to standing in the rear-leg lift. The camera lowers slightly for the floor freeze and rises smoothly with her recovery.\n\nFrom 00:05.000 to 00:07.500, covering beats 9-12, she performs the raised-knee horizontal-arm pose, lands in the low directional push, rises through the deep squat arm sweep, and shifts into the lateral low stance with one arm extending sharply sideways.\n\nFrom 00:07.500 to 00:10.000, covering beats 13-16, she moves through the seated floor lean, powers upward into the standing arm extension, performs the final knee lift with both arms raised, and finishes in the wide diagonal reach. She holds the final pose through 00:10.000 as her hair settles and her chest rises subtly.\n\nFoot contacts, weight transfers, knee bends, hair swing, fabric folds, and floor interaction remain physically believable. The movement stays fluid between poses rather than snapping like separate still images.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nClean studio room tone throughout, with soft sneaker scuffs, light fabric movement, controlled breathing, and soft floor contacts synchronized to the steps. No dialogue, crowd noise, or music leakage.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nA precise instrumental electronic dance track at 96 BPM, with a strong kick on each of the 16 beats, tight percussion, and a restrained bass pulse. No vocals; the track resolves cleanly on the final held pose."], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "text"}, "name": "text", "label": "text", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "text"}], "flags": {}, "type": "Text", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#653", "size": [400, 200], "pos": [18.57094955444336, 1244.722412109375], "id": 27, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "Text"}, "order": 15}, {"showAdvanced": false, "outputs": [{"name": "width", "links": [22], "label": "width", "type": "